    "result_text": "Confirmed \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract, `AuditLogCapture` is a helper). The full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field on the owner response, derived from the locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `timezone` property (read-only string) to the Owner schema, right after `locality`. `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec at build time, so the field had to be declared here first.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", expression = \"java(timezone(owner))\")` alongside the existing `locality` mapping, plus a `REGION_TIMEZONE` table (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`) and a `timezone(Owner)` method. It reuses the existing `locality(owner)` derivation as the key, so the two fields stay consistent by construction; regions not in the table (e.g. `UNKNOWN`) yield `null` (absent), matching the pattern used for other optional derived fields.\n\n**Verification:** `coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` passes (`$.locality` = `NSW`, `$.timezone` = `Australia/Sydney`), and `./mvnw test` reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures/errors.",
